WEBVTT

00:33:28.297 --> 00:33:30.016
AG: Take Scott Krumrei.

00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:31.222
A few years ago,

00:33:31.246 --> 00:33:33.571
Scott would have had
the odds stacked against him

00:33:33.595 --> 00:33:34.912
in a traditional interview.

00:33:34.936 --> 00:33:37.964
SK: And you look at just
about any other job posting out there,

00:33:37.988 --> 00:33:41.234
and it is, "We want a bachelor's degree
or equivalent experience,"

00:33:41.258 --> 00:33:43.248
which I absolutely did not have.

00:33:43.861 --> 00:33:46.457
AG: Scott had taken
some machine classes in high school

00:33:46.481 --> 00:33:48.473
and did two years of vocational welding,

00:33:48.497 --> 00:33:50.767
but he didn't have a college degree.

00:33:50.791 --> 00:33:54.489
When he saw that the job requirements
at Menlo didn't include prior experience

00:33:54.513 --> 00:33:55.704
or higher education,

00:33:55.728 --> 00:33:57.648
he knew he had a chance,

00:33:57.672 --> 00:33:59.986
because Menlo was looking
for something different